<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gaurinath Singha</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. 1780–1795</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gaurinath Singha was king of the Ahom kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/assam">Assam</a> from 1780 to 1795, in the worst years of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moamoria-rebellion">Moamoria rebellion</a>. Driven from his capital by the rebels, he fled to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guwahati">Guwahati</a> and in 1792 asked the British <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-india-company">East India Company</a> for help; a small force under Captain Thomas Welsh restored his authority before being recalled in 1794. In the same year he moved the capital from Rangpur to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jorhat">Jorhat</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gaurinath-singha.jpg" alt="Gaurinath Singha" width="320" height="156" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CNG Coins · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Assam_(Ahom_Kingdom)._Gaurinatha_Simha._AD_1780-1796.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
